    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d745-a5">

                <pb facs="0877" n="759" sameAs="frus:frus1928v02/pg759"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#small-caps">annex d</hi></head>
                <p rendition="#center"><hi rendition="#italic">Règlement d’Organisation
                        Judiciaire</hi></p>
                <p rendition="#center"><hi rendition="#small-caps">Title I</hi>.—<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Chapter 1</hi></p>
                <p rendition="#center"><hi rendition="#small-caps">Article</hi> 3</p>
                <table cols="2" rows="5">
                    <row role="label">
                        <cell><hi rendition="#italic">Present Text</hi></cell>
                        <cell><hi rendition="#italic">Proposed Text</hi></cell>
                    </row>
                    <row>
                        <cell>There shall be at Alexandria a Court of Appeals composed of eleven
                            magistrates—four natives and seven foreigners.</cell>
                        <cell>There shall be a Court of Appeals that may have its seat either at
                            Alexandria or Cairo and which shall consist of not less than eleven
                            magistrates—four Egyptians and seven foreigners.</cell>
                    </row>
                    <pb facs="0878" n="760" xml:id="pg760"/>
                    <row>
                        <cell>One of the foreign justices shall preside and have the title of vice
                            president. He shall be elected by an absolute majority of the foreign
                            and native members of the Court.</cell>
                        <cell/>
                    </row>
                    <row>
                        <cell>The judgments of the Court of Appeals shall be handed down by five
                            justices, of whom three shall be foreigners and two natives.</cell>
                        <cell>The judgments of the Court of Appeals shall be handed down by five
                            justices, of whom three shall be foreigners and two Egyptians, except in
                            cases of appeals from judgments of the Tribunal of Summary Jurisdiction
                            in possessory actions and replevin or of orders issued by the Tribunal
                            of Reference.</cell>
                    </row>
                    <row>
                        <cell/>
                        <cell>In the above-mentioned cases the judgments shall be handed down by
                            three justices—two foreigners and one Egyptian.</cell>
                    </row>
                </table>
            </div>
        </body>
